    "TickZen database STORAGE-UNIT CONTRACT. One entry per `table.column` that the ticker pages read.",
    "The unit of a stored value is a property of the COLUMN, never of its magnitude: consumers must look it up here and must not guess.",
    "Identical copies live in both repos (tickzen-github/database/column_units.json and Tickzen-Tickers-page-Implementation/.../lib/column-units.json); tests assert they match.",
    "Units: fraction (0.12 = 12%), percent_points (12 = 12%), ratio (multiple, 1.5 = 1.5x), days, score (0-100 scale), unit_interval (0-1 scale, not a percent), usd (currency amount), usd_per_share, count, text, date.",
    "NOTE the same logical metric differs by table (e.g. debt_to_equity is percent_points in fundamental_data but a ratio in peer_comparison_data) - that is why the key includes the table."
